Practical 1:
Exploring Ethical Case Studies in AI Systems Using Python

Aim: To explore an ethical case study of an AI-based student selection system and identify possible issues related to bias and fairness.

Problem Statement Consider an AI system that selects students for a program based on their scores.

We will examine whether the selection results are fair across different genders. 
Dataset Student Gender Score Decision Asha F 85 Selected Rahul M 80 Selected Priya F Amit M 75 Rejected 90 Selected Neha F 82 Selected Vikas M 88 Selected

Python Program # Practical: 

Exploring Ethical Case Studies in AI Systems

import pandas as pd  
Create dataset data = {
    "Student": ["Asha", "Rahul", "Priya", "Amit", "Neha", "Vikas"],
    "Gender": ["F", "M", "F", "M", "F", "M"],
    "Score": [85, 80, 90, 75, 82, 88]
    }
  df = pd.DataFrame(data)
  # AI selection rule
  # Students with score >= 80 are selected 
  df["Decision"] = df["Score"].apply( lambda x: "Selected" if x >= 80 else "Rejected" )
  print("Student Selection Results:")
  print(df)
  # Calculate selection rate for each gender
  selection_rate = df.groupby("Gender")["Decision"].apply( lambda x: (x == "Selected").mean() * 100 1 )
  print("\nSelection Rate by Gender:")
  print(selection_rate)
  # Display selected and rejected students
  print("\nSelected Students:")
  print(df[df["Decision"] == "Selected"])
  print("\nRejected Students:")
  print(df[df["Decision"] == "Rejected"])
  
